<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>VardeFM third-party licenses</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 60em; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1em; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1em; }
  li { margin: 0.2em 0; }
  .by { color: #555; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licenses</h1>
<p>VardeFM itself is licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE).
The vardefm program includes the following libraries, under these licenses.
The source of every Rust crate is available on <a href="https://crates.io">crates.io</a>.</p>

<p>Where a crate ships no license file that could be read, the standard license text is
shown. The copyright holders are then the crate's authors as listed below, or those named
under <a href="#holders">Additional copyright notices</a>.</p>

<h2>Licenses used</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li>{{name}}</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="license-{{@index}}">{{name}}</h2>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}
{{#if crate.source}}
  <li><a href="https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a>{{#if crate.authors}} <span class="by">by {{#each crate.authors}}{{#unless @first}}, {{/unless}}{{this}}{{/each}}</span>{{else}}{{#if crate.repository}} <span class="by">(<a href="{{crate.repository}}">source</a>)</span>{{/if}}{{/if}}</li>
{{/if}}
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}

<h2 id="holders">Additional copyright notices</h2>
<ul>
  <li>windows, windows-* and windows_* crates (<a href="https://github.com/microsoft/windows-rs">windows-rs</a>): Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.</li>
  <li>objc2, objc2-* crates (<a href="https://github.com/madsmtm/objc2">objc2</a>): Copyright Mads Marquart.</li>
</ul>

